## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle clock skew and scheduling drift in a regulated batch pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Clock synchronization, idempotent batch processing, per-tenant isolation
- Safe backfill, read-after-write consistency, and rollback criteria
- Clear observability and thresholds for cross-region workloads

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo dedupe example
async function processBatch(batchId, tenantId, payload){
  const key = `${batchId}:${tenantId}`;
  const exists = await redis.setnx(`dedup:${key}`, '1');
  if(!exists) return; // already processed
  // process
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the backfill strategy without impacting live tenants?
- What if clock drift persists after NTP sync—what changes to the plan would you add?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical SRE skills: incident triage, region-aware rollouts, backpressure, circuit breaking, and rollback discipline beyond basic incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region latency analysis
- Cache stampede mitigation
- Per-region deployment strategies (canary, rollouts)
- Safe rollback criteria and instrumentation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple circuit breaker (pseudo)
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold) { this.open = false; this.failures = 0; this.threshold = threshold; }
  onFailure() { this.failures++; if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.open = true; }
  allow() { return !this.open; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to a service mesh with traffic shifting?
- How would you verify rollback correctness across all regions post-incident?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region backpressure, ordering guarantees, and safe rollback in production systems with tight SLOs.

## Key Concepts

- Region-aware throttling
- Delivery guarantees and ordering
- Cross-region coordination
- Feature flags and safe rollbacks
- Observability and synthetic testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: region-aware token bucket release
function shouldRelease(region, tokens, backlog) {
  if (tokens[region] <= 0) return false;
  if (backlog[region] > TARGET_BACKLOG) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the backpressure under simulated spikes without affecting live data?
- What metrics would you capture to validate SLO compliance during failover?
